# Granulation and source-unit follow-up (exploratory)
GSE103667 Pmp22 source TE values decrease in both replicate labels; its seven RefSeq rows are repeated mappings, not independent isoforms/replicates. Source Methods describe TE on log10 plotting scale but deposited values include0 and values>1000; retain source units and distinguish the linear-ratio interpretation from direct differences until source-table semantics are resolved. Both imply decreased TE.
Namkoong et al already established that broad translational suppression does not necessarily imply granule recruitment. A target-level RNA-granule test can distinguish that alternative for PMP22. GSE90869 has24 samples and three independent biological replicates of ER-stress fractionation according to source text, but RG and TE are the same source study, not independent biological validation. Processed three count tables are available. Analyze Pmp22 alongside annotation-independent universe, RNA composition and known source positive controls Xiap/Ago3/Creb1. Require valid counts and inspect spike-in availability before absolute %RG claims. Without spike normalization, only relative partitioning is estimable; do not replace missing source calibration with a measured-zero or promise a causal granule mechanism. This is exploratory follow-up, not a new prospective confirmation.
